'' RUN: 'C( c1 )' spelt out, over a type whose only declared constructor takes a long, binds
'' to the IMPLICIT copy constructor its string field gives it -- so do 'C( f( ) )' (copied
'' from the temporary, which is then destroyed), 'C( *pc )', and 'H( h1 )' where the string
'' is a field's. PickCtor sees declared constructors only, so each declined silently
'' (lowervarinit.bas, "statements not lowered") and left the variable default-constructed:
'' 0 and an empty string. Output identical to fbc-modern's, destructor order included.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/ctor-implicit-copy-call.bas -o tests/codegen/ctorimplcopy.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/ctorimplcopy.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/ctorimplcopy.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ctor 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 s1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ctor 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7 s7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 s1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  5 n5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: end
